Well, no.

As others have said down-thread, a parenthetical
portion of a sentence is just a clarification; the
sentence should still have an intact meaning if that
parenthetical part is removed. Without the
parenthetical part, the sentence reads

Walking or squeezing past a boulder in Sokoban.

Obviously, "walking" per se is not the issue, it is
"walking past a boulder".

What the parenthetical part clarifies is that
walking past a boulder is something only referring
to the actions of a giant.

That is unsurprising, since no other creature can
walk past a boulder (except the naked PC, who is
"squeezing", not "walking", thus the rest of the
sentence).

